; Anomaly Coop - stock Anomaly scripts that stay on the host (rulings F2-28, F2-29), read by the engine after
; configs\coop_route.ltx like every coop_route_*.ltx (same sections and rules, see there).
;
; GENERATED by tools\gen_route_world.lua - do not edit by hand. Rerun it after a GAMMA or Anomaly update or a
; change of the other route files, then run tools\test_lua.cmd:
;   set GAMMA_SCRIPTS=E:\AnomalyCoopGamma\gamedata\scripts&& temp\lua\runlua.exe tools\gen_route_world.lua
; Since F2 T10 a script without a rule follows its callback (actor_* owner: runs on a client, review R5 I4); before,
; it was host. A script below calls a world function (alife():create / alife_create / ..._release, create_squad,
; SIMBOARD, give_info / disable_info, relations, transfer_item, :kill, sim:release, safe_release_manager.release,
; xr_logic.switch_to_section), has no rule of its own and did not run on a client before T10, so it keeps that:
; until the call router (F2 T12) gates world calls a client running it could
; duplicate items, artefacts or infos.
; A client that needs one of them shows it in coop_status ([coop] routes: most skipped / latest new skips). Give
; that script its own rule in a configs\coop_compat_<mod>.ltx: those are read last and win over this file, and
; the next run of the generator leaves the script out.
; Generated 2026-10-23 from ..\anomaly-ref\unpacked\scripts + engine\gamedata\scripts + gamedata\scripts:
;   530 scripts, 184 call world functions, 72 of those have a rule; 112 below (54 register a handler
;   literally, the others are routed when somebody else registers their functions).
; Comment of a line: world calls in the file | literal registrations (unique_call / time_event: timers).

